{
 "Actor, Judge, or Teacher? · REAL Lab Blog": "Actor, Judge, or Teacher? · REAL Lab 博客",
 "Decision models such as JEV struggle to act on tasks whose subgoals must be met in order, yet judged in hindsight they teach a 1.5B policy that outperforms them: 72.8% → 82.9% on ALFWorld and 56.8% → 71.4% on WebShop.": "JEV 这类决策模型在子目标必须按顺序完成的任务上很难自己执行好，但让它们事后评判，教出的 1.5B 策略反而超过了它们：ALFWorld 上 72.8% → 82.9%，WebShop 上 56.8% → 71.4%。",
 "A decision model that acts poorly can still teach well, if it is asked whether each action helped and shown the whole trajectory.": "决策模型自己执行得不好，也可能教得好，前提是问它每个动作有没有帮助，并让它看到完整轨迹。",
 "<a href=\"../../blog.html\">Blog</a><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>November 22, 2026</span><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>Agentic AI · Reinforcement learning</span><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>14 min read</span>": "<a href=\"../../blog.html\">博客</a><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>2026 年 11 月 22 日</span><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>智能体 · 强化学习</span><span class=\"dot\"></span><span>阅读约 14 分钟</span>",
 "Decision models answer a question with a choice and a probability, so the same model can pick an agent's actions, grade them, or teach a policy. We find that a model which acts poorly can still teach well, as long as it is asked the right question and shown the whole trajectory.": "决策模型针对一个问题给出一个选项和对应的概率，所以同一个模型既可以替智能体选动作，也可以给动作打分，还可以指导策略训练。我们发现，一个自己执行得不好的模型照样可以当好老师，只要问对问题，并让它看到完整轨迹。",
 "<sup>1</sup>Zhejiang University <sup>2</sup>Baidu Inc. · *Equal contribution †Corresponding author": "<sup>1</sup>浙江大学 <sup>2</sup>百度 · *同等贡献 †通讯作者",
 "<a href=\"#roles\"><span class=\"n\">1</span>Three ways to ask</a>": "<a href=\"#roles\"><span class=\"n\">1</span>三种问法</a>",
 "<a href=\"#actor\"><span class=\"n\">2</span>As an actor</a>": "<a href=\"#actor\"><span class=\"n\">2</span>作为执行者</a>",
 "<a href=\"#actor-order\">Ordered subgoals</a>": "<a href=\"#actor-order\">有序子目标</a>",
 "<a href=\"#actor-distract\">Distraction, not ignorance</a>": "<a href=\"#actor-distract\">是分心，不是不会</a>",
 "<a href=\"#judge\"><span class=\"n\">3</span>As a judge</a>": "<a href=\"#judge\"><span class=\"n\">3</span>作为裁判</a>",
 "<a href=\"#judge-question\">Ask about the action</a>": "<a href=\"#judge-question\">问动作本身</a>",
 "<a href=\"#judge-context\">Show the whole trajectory</a>": "<a href=\"#judge-context\">给出完整轨迹</a>",
 "<a href=\"#teacher\"><span class=\"n\">4</span>As a teacher</a>": "<a href=\"#teacher\"><span class=\"n\">4</span>作为老师</a>",
 "<a href=\"#teacher-signal\">From scores to advantages</a>": "<a href=\"#teacher-signal\">从得分到优势</a>",
 "<a href=\"#teacher-results\">Results</a>": "<a href=\"#teacher-results\">结果</a>",
 "<a href=\"#teacher-surpass\">Learning beyond the teacher</a>": "<a href=\"#teacher-surpass\">学生超过老师</a>",
 "<a href=\"#takeaways\"><span class=\"n\">5</span>Takeaways</a>": "<a href=\"#takeaways\"><span class=\"n\">5</span>几点结论</a>",
 "<a href=\"#roles\">Three ways to ask a decision model</a>": "<a href=\"#roles\">向决策模型提问的三种方式</a>",
 "<a href=\"#actor\">As an actor</a>": "<a href=\"#actor\">作为执行者</a>",
 "<a href=\"#judge\">As a judge</a>": "<a href=\"#judge\">作为裁判</a>",
 "<a href=\"#teacher\">As a teacher</a>": "<a href=\"#teacher\">作为老师</a>",
 "<a href=\"#takeaways\">Takeaways</a>": "<a href=\"#takeaways\">几点结论</a>",
 "A <em>decision model</em> answers a question about a context with a typed output, such as a choice among options with a probability for each, instead of free text. Because any question can be asked about any state, one model can choose an agent's next action, evaluate an action already taken, or score every action of a policy during reinforcement learning. So far these models have mostly been judged by how well they act.": "<em>决策模型</em>针对给定的上下文回答一个问题，输出的是结构化结果而不是自由文本，比如从几个选项中选一个，并给出每个选项的概率。任何状态下都可以问任何问题，所以同一个模型既能选择智能体的下一步动作，也能评估已经做过的动作，还能在强化学习中给策略的每个动作打分。到目前为止，人们评价这类模型主要看它执行得好不好。",
 "We asked whether a model that acts poorly can still teach well. On ALFWorld, JEV completes <strong>42.9%</strong> of tasks when it chooses the actions itself. Used instead to score each action of a 1.5B policy during GRPO training, it raises that policy's success over GRPO alone from 72.8% to <strong>82.9%</strong> on the same tasks, and from 56.8% to <strong>71.4%</strong> on WebShop. <strong>The difference comes from timing: an actor must anticipate consequences, whereas a judge that reads the finished episode can see them.</strong>": "我们想知道：执行得不好的模型，能不能教得好？在 ALFWorld 上，JEV 自己选动作时只完成 <strong>42.9%</strong> 的任务。换个用法，让它在 GRPO 训练中给 1.5B 策略的每个动作打分，同一批任务上的成功率就从只用 GRPO 的 72.8% 提高到 <strong>82.9%</strong>，WebShop 上从 56.8% 提高到 <strong>71.4%</strong>。<strong>差别在于时机：执行者必须提前预判后果，而读完整个回合的裁判能直接看到后果。</strong>",
 "The benefit is not automatic. It appears only when the model is asked whether each action <em>helped achieve the goal</em>, rather than whether the task will succeed, and only when it sees the <em>whole trajectory</em> rather than the steps leading up to the action. Queried this way after each episode, a frozen decision model provides step-level supervision for 22 to 30 USD of API calls per training run, with no step labels and no learned critic.": "这种收益不是自动得来的。只有问模型每个动作是否<em>有助于达成目标</em>，而不是问任务会不会成功，并且让它看到<em>完整轨迹</em>，而不只是这个动作之前的步骤，收益才会出现。按这种方式在每个回合结束后查询，一个冻结的决策模型就能提供步级监督，每次训练的 API 费用为 22 到 30 美元，既不需要步级标注，也不需要训练 critic。",
 "<span class=\"n\">1</span>Three ways to ask a decision model": "<span class=\"n\">1</span>向决策模型提问的三种方式",
 "A decision model takes a <em>question</em> and a <em>context</em>. For a multiple-choice question it selects an option and assigns a probability to every option; for a yes/no question it returns one score in [0, 1]. We query the same model in three roles that differ only in what it is asked and how its answer is used.": "决策模型的输入是一个<em>问题</em>和一段<em>上下文</em>。遇到选择题，它选出一个选项，并给每个选项分配概率；遇到是非题，它返回 [0, 1] 区间内的一个分数。我们让同一个模型扮演三种角色，区别只在于问它什么、怎么使用它的回答。",
 "<span class=\"role-a\">Actor.</span> At each step the model picks the next action from the valid commands, given the goal, the history and the current observation. The choice is executed.": "<span class=\"role-a\">执行者。</span>每一步，模型根据目标、历史和当前观测，从合法命令中选出下一步动作，然后执行这个动作。",
 "<span class=\"role-j\">Judge.</span> The model scores each action of a recorded trajectory. We vary what it sees, the trajectory up to the action (<em>Prefix</em>) or the whole trajectory (<em>Hindsight</em>), and what it is asked, whether the task will succeed after the action (<em>Value</em>) or whether the action helped achieve the goal (<em>Progress</em>).": "<span class=\"role-j\">裁判。</span>模型给一条已记录轨迹中的每个动作打分。我们改变两点。一是它能看到的内容：截至这个动作的前缀（<em>Prefix</em>），或事后看到的完整轨迹（<em>Hindsight</em>）。二是问它的问题：做完这个动作后任务能否成功（<em>Value</em>），或这个动作是否推动了目标的达成（<em>Progress</em>）。",
 "<span class=\"role-t\">Teacher.</span> The model scores the actions of the policy being trained, and the scores enter GRPO as step-level credit. It stays frozen and is not used at test time.": "<span class=\"role-t\">老师。</span>模型给正在训练的策略的动作打分，分数作为步级的信用分配信号加入 GRPO。模型本身保持冻结，测试时不使用。",
 "<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-1\">Figure 1</a> plays the three roles on the paper's running example: put a heated mug on a table.": "<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-1\">图 1</a>用论文中贯穿始终的例子演示这三种角色：把加热过的杯子放到桌上。",
 "<span class=\"m1-tn\">1</span>Actor<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>": "<span class=\"m1-tn\">1</span>执行者<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>",
 "<span class=\"m1-tn\">2</span>Judge<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>": "<span class=\"m1-tn\">2</span>裁判<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>",
 "<span class=\"m1-tn\">3</span>Teacher<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>": "<span class=\"m1-tn\">3</span>老师<i class=\"m1-prog\"></i>",
 "<b>Actor</b><span>picks the next action</span>": "<b>执行者</b><span>选择下一步动作</span>",
 "<b>Judge</b><span>scores a recorded action</span>": "<b>裁判</b><span>给已记录的动作打分</span>",
 "Recorded episode: put a heated mug in the cabinet": "已记录的回合：把加热过的杯子放进柜子",
 "<b>Teacher</b><span>scores the policy's own rollouts</span>": "<b>老师</b><span>给策略自己的 rollout 打分</span>",
 "Decision model": "决策模型",
 "question + context → typed answer. Here JEV, one of the six models we test.": "问题 + 上下文 → 结构化回答。这里用的是 JEV，我们测试的六个模型之一。",
 "Choice probabilities": "各选项的概率",
 "Easier subgoal first: the task is left incomplete.": "先完成了较容易的子目标，任务因此没能完成。",
 "Same question; seeing the mug heated shows why it mattered.": "问题相同；看到后面加热了杯子，就明白这一步为什么重要。",
 "The no-op is pushed down; taking the cold mug back is credited.": "无效动作的优势被压低；取回冷杯子这一步得到肯定。",
 "<b>Figure 1.</b> One decision model, queried three ways on heated-mug tasks. <b>Actor:</b> JEV’s choice probabilities, averaged over 116 states in which the object still needs heating, cleaning or cooling. <b>Judge:</b> JEV’s score for step 9 of a recorded episode, seeing first the steps up to it and then the whole episode (paper Table 9). <b>Teacher:</b> illustrative scores from the paper’s Figure 1, centred within the group and added to GRPO’s outcome advantage. Use the tabs to jump to a role.": "<b>图 1</b> 同一个决策模型在加热杯子类任务上的三种用法。<b>执行者：</b>JEV 在 116 个状态上的平均选项概率，这些状态中物体仍需加热、清洗或冷却。<b>裁判：</b>JEV 给一个已记录回合第 9 步的打分，先只看到截至这一步的轨迹，再看到完整回合（论文表 9）。<b>老师：</b>取自论文图 1 的示意分数，在组内中心化后加到 GRPO 的结果优势上。点击上方标签可跳到对应角色。",
 "We evaluate six models that answer questions in this form. Three are released as <strong>dedicated decision models</strong> and are queried through their own decision APIs. The other three are <strong>general LLMs</strong> asked the same questions, either by prompting for a JSON answer or by reading the first-token probabilities of the valid answer labels. Two of these general LLMs are the base models of Decider v1.2 and GPT Decisions, so each dedicated model can be compared with its own base model.": "我们评测了六个能以这种形式回答问题的模型。其中三个以<strong>专用决策模型</strong>的形式发布，通过各自的决策 API 调用。另外三个是<strong>通用大模型</strong>，问它们同样的问题，或在提示中要求输出 JSON 答案，或读取合法答案标签的首 token 概率。这三个通用大模型里，有两个分别是 Decider v1.2 和 GPT Decisions 的基座模型，因此这两个专用模型都可以和各自的基座模型直接比较。",
 "Model": "模型",
 "Base LLM": "基座模型",
 "How the decision interface is obtained": "决策接口的获得方式",
 "Access": "访问方式",
 "undisclosed": "未公开",
 "API only": "仅 API",
 "full fine-tuning": "全参数微调",
 "open weights": "开放权重",
 "prompting (JSON answer)": "提示（JSON 答案）",
 "constrained readout (first-token probabilities)": "约束读取（首 token 概率）",
 "We use two text environments in which some requirements must be met in a fixed order. In <strong>ALFWorld</strong> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-alfworld\">[1]</a>, an agent completes household goals with commands such as <code>go to</code>, <code>take</code> and <code>heat</code>. Its <em>Clean</em>, <em>Heat</em> and <em>Cool</em> tasks have a dependency: the object's state must change before it is placed. <em>Pick2</em> also has two requirements, two objects to place, but they can be met in either order. In <strong>WebShop</strong> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-webshop\">[2]</a>, an agent searches a catalogue and must select the required options before it buys.": "我们使用两个文本环境，环境中有些要求必须按固定顺序满足。在 <strong>ALFWorld</strong> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-alfworld\">[1]</a> 中，智能体用 <code>go to</code>、<code>take</code>、<code>heat</code> 等命令完成家务目标。<em>Clean</em>、<em>Heat</em> 和 <em>Cool</em> 三类任务存在依赖：物体必须先改变状态，才能放置。<em>Pick2</em> 同样有两个要求，即放置两个物体，但先后顺序不限。在 <strong>WebShop</strong> <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-webshop\">[2]</a> 中，智能体在商品目录中搜索，下单前必须选好要求的选项。",
 "<span class=\"n\">2</span>As an actor, an easier subgoal gets in the way": "<span class=\"n\">2</span>作为执行者：较容易的子目标会碍事",
 "Finding 1": "发现 1",
 "As actors, all six models struggle when one subgoal must be completed before another: an easier subgoal draws them away from the one that has to come first.": "作为执行者，只要一个子目标必须先于另一个完成，六个模型都表现吃力：较容易的子目标会把它们从必须先做的那个子目标上引开。",
 "Ordered subgoals are where acting breaks": "有序子目标是执行的短板",
 "Every model succeeds far less often on tasks with a dependency than on tasks without one (<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-2\">Figure 2</a>). JEV completes 70.8% of <em>Pick2</em> tasks but at most 18.8% of each dependent task type. Decider v1.2, the strongest actor overall at 63.6%, completes only 18.8% of <em>Heat</em> tasks. Because <em>Pick2</em> also has two subgoals, the gap points to their <em>order</em> rather than their number as the difficulty.": "所有模型在有依赖的任务上，成功率都远低于没有依赖的任务（<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-2\">图 2</a>）。JEV 能完成 70.8% 的 <em>Pick2</em> 任务，但在每一类依赖任务上最多只完成 18.8%。Decider v1.2 是整体最强的执行者（63.6%），在 <em>Heat</em> 任务上也只完成 18.8%。<em>Pick2</em> 同样有两个子目标，可见难点在于子目标的<em>顺序</em>，而不是数量。",
 "ALFWorld, acting": "ALFWorld，执行",
 "Actor success rate by task type": "各任务类型上执行者的成功率",
 "All task types": "全部任务类型",
 "Pick2 vs dependent": "Pick2 对比依赖任务",
 "<b>Figure 2.</b> Success rates (%) of the six models acting on ALFWorld, one run per task on the evaluation tasks later used for the trained policies. <i>Pick2</i> and the three dependent types both have two subgoals; only the dependent ones fix their order. Switch to “Pick2 vs dependent” to compare those directly; hover a cell for its value.": "<b>图 2</b> 六个模型在 ALFWorld 上作为执行者的成功率（%）。评估任务与后文训练策略所用的相同，每个任务运行一次。<i>Pick2</i> 和三类依赖任务都有两个子目标，只有依赖任务规定了先后顺序。切换到“Pick2 对比依赖任务”可直接比较二者；鼠标悬停在单元格上可查看数值。",
 "The failed episodes show how the order is broken. Holding the mug at the table, the actor can place it in one action, or walk to the microwave, heat it and come back. In many failures it places the unheated mug and the task can no longer be completed as intended.": "从失败的回合可以看出顺序是怎么出错的。拿着杯子站在桌边时，执行者可以一步把杯子放下，也可以走到微波炉把杯子加热再回来。很多失败案例里，它直接放下了未加热的杯子，任务就无法按要求完成了。",
 "Distraction, not ignorance": "是分心，不是不会",
 "We collected 116 states, from 66 tasks, in which a single action would satisfy the easier subgoal while the required one was still unmet, and queried each actor there under two goals that differ only in the easier subgoal, for example “put a heated mug on the side table” versus “heat a mug”. Everything else, including the history, observation, candidate actions and remaining budget, is identical.": "我们从 66 个任务中收集了 116 个状态：在这些状态下，一个动作就能满足较容易的子目标，而必须先完成的子目标还没有达成。我们在每个状态上用两个目标分别询问执行者，两个目标只差较容易的那个子目标，例如“把加热过的杯子放到边桌上”和“加热杯子”。其余内容，包括历史、观测、候选动作和剩余步数预算，完全相同。",
 "<strong>With the full goal, JEV puts 63.8% of its probability on the easier subgoal and 14.6% on the step that must come first; without it, these become 2.5% and 77.6%</strong> (<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-3\">Figure 3</a>, left). All six actors shift the same way. They know the required step; the easier subgoal pulls probability away from it. Reminding them of the dependency barely helps: a generic hint changes success by −2.8 to +5.2 points, and adding a worked ordering example helps some models but not all (Figure 3, right).": "<strong>给出完整目标时，JEV 把 63.8% 的概率放在较容易的子目标上，只有 14.6% 放在必须先做的那一步；去掉较容易的子目标后，两者变为 2.5% 和 77.6%</strong>（<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-3\">图 3</a> 左）。六个执行者的变化方向都一样。它们知道该做哪一步，只是较容易的子目标把概率吸走了。提醒它们注意依赖关系几乎没用：一条通用提示只让成功率变化 −2.8 到 +5.2 个百分点；再加上一个示范正确顺序的例子，只对部分模型有效（图 3 右）。",
 "JEV, 116 states": "JEV，116 个状态",
 "Where the probability goes": "概率分给了谁",
 "Share of JEV's probability by action type, %": "JEV 的概率在各类动作上的占比（%）",
 "Full goal": "完整目标",
 "Without the easier subgoal": "去掉较容易的子目标",
 "Same 116 states, continued to the end": "同样的 116 个状态，继续执行到结束",
 "Success with an ordering example in the prompt": "提示中加入顺序示例后的成功率",
 "Original prompt → hint plus a heated-mug example, %": "原提示 → 依赖提示加一个加热杯子的示例（%）",
 "<b>Figure 3.</b> <b>Left:</b> JEV's action probabilities, grouped into the step toward the subgoal that must come first, the action that completes the easier subgoal, and everything else, with and without the easier subgoal in the goal. <b>Right:</b> success when each episode continues under the original prompt versus a dependency hint plus an ordering example. GPT Luna, which changes little, is omitted because the paper does not report its values in the text.": "<b>图 3</b> <b>左：</b>JEV 的动作概率，分为三组：推进必须先完成的子目标的一步、完成较容易子目标的动作、其他动作；分别给出目标中包含和不包含较容易子目标时的结果。<b>右：</b>每个回合分别在原提示下和在“依赖提示 + 顺序示例”下继续执行时的成功率。GPT Luna 变化不大，论文正文没有给出它的数值，因此图中省略。",
 "Acting correctly here requires anticipating that the easy action leaves the task unfinished <em>before</em> any consequence is visible. A judge evaluates the action after its consequences have occurred, which is where the next section starts.": "要在这里做对，执行者必须在任何后果显现<em>之前</em>就预判到：这个简单动作会让任务无法完成。裁判则是在动作的后果出现之后才评估它，下一节就从这里讲起。",
 "<span class=\"n\">3</span>As a judge, the question and the context decide": "<span class=\"n\">3</span>作为裁判：关键在问什么、看什么",
 "Finding 2": "发现 2",
 "The same models can recognise contributions they overlook as actors. Seeing the whole trajectory reveals how earlier actions feed later progress, and asking whether each action helped separates those actions from ones that change nothing.": "同样的模型作为执行者时会忽略一些动作的贡献，作为裁判却能识别出来。看到完整轨迹，就能看出前面的动作怎样促成后面的进展；问每个动作是否有帮助，就能把这些动作和毫无作用的动作区分开。",
 "We reused the successful continuations from the 116 states and asked each judge whether the first action taken from the diagnostic state helped achieve the goal, with outcome labels masked. Seeing the whole trajectory instead of the prefix raises the mean score of these actions for all six models; for JEV it goes from 0.41 to 0.59. That raises two questions: does a full trajectory simply make every action look good, and what does the judge actually gain from it?": "我们复用了从这 116 个状态出发的成功后续轨迹，屏蔽结果标签，问每个裁判：从诊断状态出发执行的第一个动作是否有助于达成目标。把前缀换成完整轨迹后，六个模型给这些动作的平均分都提高了，JEV 从 0.41 升到 0.59。由此引出两个问题：完整轨迹是不是只会让每个动作都显得不错？裁判到底从中得到了什么？",
 "Ask whether the action helped, not whether the task will succeed": "问动作有没有帮助，而不是任务会不会成功",
 "We labelled actions in 462 ALFWorld trajectories as <em>milestones</em>, which achieve a subgoal, <em>no-ops</em>, which leave the environment unchanged, and <em>other</em>. With the whole trajectory visible, the <em>Value</em> question gives the three groups almost the same score: if the episode ends in success, every action in it “leads to success”. The <em>Progress</em> question spreads them apart for every model (<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-4\">Figure 4</a>). For JEV, within a trajectory, Progress scores milestones 0.36 above no-ops, against 0.05 for Value, and it ranks more milestones among each trajectory's top-scored actions, by 8.0 to 16.0 points.": "我们把 462 条 ALFWorld 轨迹中的动作标为三类：<em>里程碑</em>（达成某个子目标）、<em>无效动作</em>（环境没有变化）和<em>其他</em>。能看到完整轨迹时，<em>Value</em> 问题给三类动作的分数几乎一样：只要回合最终成功，其中每个动作都“通向成功”。<em>Progress</em> 问题则在所有模型上都把三类拉开了（<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-4\">图 4</a>）。以 JEV 为例，在同一条轨迹内，Progress 给里程碑的分数比无效动作高 0.36，Value 只高 0.05；Progress 还能把更多里程碑排进每条轨迹得分最高的那批动作里，多出 8.0 到 16.0 个百分点。",
 "ALFWorld, 462 trajectories, Hindsight context": "ALFWorld，462 条轨迹，Hindsight 上下文",
 "Mean action score by action type": "各类动作的平均得分",
 "<b>Figure 4.</b> Mean Hindsight scores for milestone, other and no-op actions under the two questions; scores are averaged within each trajectory, then across trajectories. The bracket shows the difference between the milestone and no-op means. Pick a judge to compare; Progress separates the groups for all six.": "<b>图 4</b> 两种问题下里程碑、其他和无效动作的 Hindsight 平均得分；先在每条轨迹内平均，再对所有轨迹平均。括线标出里程碑与无效动作均值之差。可以选择不同裁判比较，六个模型上 Progress 都能把三组区分开。",
 "Show the whole trajectory": "给出完整轨迹",
 "To see what the extra context buys, we held the question fixed to Progress and revealed the trajectory step by step: the prefix, then the immediate feedback after the action, then 25%, 50%, 75% and all of what follows. Over 167 trajectories, JEV's ranking of actions within a trajectory moves by 1.95 positions on average once feedback is added, and by 3.30 positions with the full trajectory. <a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-5\">Figure 5</a> shows one of them. Drag the slider, or press play.": "为了看清更多上下文带来了什么，我们固定使用 Progress 问题，逐步展开轨迹：先是前缀，然后加上动作后的即时反馈，再加上后续部分的 25%、50%、75% 直至全部。在 167 条轨迹上，加入反馈后，JEV 对轨迹内各动作的排名平均变动 1.95 位；看到完整轨迹时，平均变动 3.30 位。<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-5\">图 5</a> 展示了其中一条，可以拖动滑块，或点击播放。",
 "JEV as a judge, Progress question": "JEV 作裁判，Progress 问题",
 "“Put a heated mug in the cabinet”: scores as more of the episode becomes visible": "“把加热过的杯子放进柜子”：随着可见的回合内容增加，各步得分的变化",
 "Visible context": "可见上下文",
 "<b>Figure 5.</b> JEV's Progress scores for all 12 actions of one episode (paper Table 9). The mug is put in the cabinet before it is heated (step 6), taken back (7), heated in the microwave (8 to 10) and put back (12). Each bar is the score of that action when the judge sees the episode up to the action, plus the immediate feedback, plus 25%, 50%, 75% or all of the remaining steps.": "<b>图 5</b> JEV 对一个回合中全部 12 个动作给出的 Progress 得分（论文表 9）。杯子在加热前就放进了柜子（第 6 步），随后取回（7），用微波炉加热（8 到 10），再放回去（12）。每根柱子是裁判对这个动作的打分，裁判看到的内容依次为：截至这个动作的回合，再加上即时反馈，再加上其余步骤的 25%、50%、75% 或全部。",
 "Under the prefix, JEV rates the premature placement (step 6) at 0.79 and going to the microwave (8) and opening it (9) at only 0.23 and 0.20, the same preference for the easier subgoal that the actor showed. Immediate feedback makes it worse: placement rises to 0.90. Only as the continuation comes into view do the microwave steps earn credit; opening the microwave reaches 0.66 once heating is visible and 0.76 with the full trajectory. The repeated <code>look</code> (step 2) stays low throughout, because the prefix alone already shows that it repeats step 1.": "只看前缀时，JEV 给过早放置（第 6 步）打 0.79，走向微波炉（8）和打开微波炉（9）却只有 0.23 和 0.20，这正是执行者表现出的那种对较容易子目标的偏好。加入即时反馈反而更糟：放置的得分升到 0.90。只有当后续步骤逐渐可见，微波炉相关的步骤才得到认可：一旦能看到加热，打开微波炉的得分升到 0.66，看到完整轨迹时为 0.76。重复的 <code>look</code>（第 2 步）始终得分很低，因为仅凭前缀就能看出它重复了第 1 步。",
 "The two dedicated decision models whose base LLM is disclosed, Decider v1.2 and GPT Decisions, also judge more accurately than that base LLM given the same question, at 28% to 43% lower cost per score.": "Decider v1.2 和 GPT Decisions 这两个公开了基座模型的专用决策模型，在同样的问题下作裁判，也比各自的基座模型更准确，每次打分的成本还低 28% 到 43%。",
 "<span class=\"n\">4</span>As a teacher, the best judge gives the best signal": "<span class=\"n\">4</span>作为老师：最好的裁判给出最好的信号",
 "Finding 3": "发现 3",
 "The judgments that best separate useful from useless actions also train the strongest policies, and the gains are largest on the tasks the teacher fails as an actor.": "最能区分有用和无用动作的评判，也训练出了最强的策略；提升最大的，恰恰是老师自己作为执行者会失败的那些任务。",
 "From scores to advantages": "从得分到优势",
 "GRPO gives every action in a rollout the same outcome advantage. For each task the policy samples a group of trajectories; after they finish, the teacher <span class=\"mi\">D</span> scores every executed action <span class=\"mi\">t</span> of every trajectory <span class=\"mi\">τ<sub>i</sub></span> from the goal and the trajectory alone, with no rewards, success labels or hidden state:": "GRPO 给一条 rollout 中的每个动作相同的结果优势。对每个任务，策略采样一组轨迹；轨迹结束后，老师 <span class=\"mi\">D</span> 只根据目标和轨迹本身，给每条轨迹 <span class=\"mi\">τ<sub>i</sub></span> 中执行过的每个动作 <span class=\"mi\">t</span> 打分，不使用奖励、成功标签或隐藏状态：",
 "The scores are centred on the mean <span class=\"mi\">s̄</span> over all scored actions in the group and added with weight λ = 0.5. They are deliberately not divided by their standard deviation, so a group in which the teacher hardly distinguishes actions receives only small adjustments. <a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-6\">Figure 6</a> shows what the teacher term does to the two rollouts from Figure 1.": "分数减去组内所有打过分的动作的均值 <span class=\"mi\">s̄</span>，再以权重 λ = 0.5 加进优势。我们有意不除以标准差，这样当老师几乎分不出动作好坏时，这一组只会得到很小的调整。<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-6\">图 6</a> 展示了老师项对图 1 中两条 rollout 的作用。",
 "Illustrative group of two rollouts": "示意：一组两条 rollout",
 "What the teacher adds to each action's advantage": "老师给每个动作的优势加了多少",
 "<b>Figure 6.</b> λ(<i>s</i> − <i>s̄</i>) for each action, using the illustrative teacher scores of Figure 1 (group mean 0.71). Bars above zero receive a larger advantage than GRPO alone would give, bars below a smaller one. The outcome advantage itself is the same for every action of a rollout, so only the teacher term distinguishes them. The paper trains with λ = 0.5.": "<b>图 6</b> 每个动作的 λ(<i>s</i> − <i>s̄</i>)，使用图 1 中的示意老师分数（组均值 0.71）。零线以上的柱子得到的优势比只用 GRPO 时更大，零线以下的更小。结果优势对一条 rollout 中的所有动作都相同，所以只有老师项能区分它们。论文训练时取 λ = 0.5。",
 "Results": "结果",
 "We train Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct with JEV as the teacher under all four combinations of question and context, and compare against GRPO with outcome rewards alone (results from GiGPO <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-gigpo\">[3]</a>). Each policy is evaluated with three seeds. <strong>Hindsight + Progress gives the highest success on both environments: 72.8% → 82.9% on ALFWorld and 56.8% → 71.4% on WebShop.</strong> It improves on every ALFWorld task type, most on <em>Cool</em> (+23.0) and <em>Look</em> (+20.7). With the prefix only, the two questions perform about the same. The ordering matches the judge analysis: under Hindsight, the Value question gives every action of an episode nearly the same score and so says little about which actions helped.": "我们以 JEV 为老师训练 Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct，覆盖问题与上下文的全部四种组合，并与只用结果奖励的 GRPO 对比（结果取自 GiGPO <a class=\"cite\" href=\"#ref-gigpo\">[3]</a>）。每个策略用三个随机种子评估。<strong>Hindsight + Progress 在两个环境上都取得最高成功率：ALFWorld 上 72.8% → 82.9%，WebShop 上 56.8% → 71.4%。</strong>它在 ALFWorld 的每类任务上都有提升，<em>Cool</em>（+23.0）和 <em>Look</em>（+20.7）提升最多。只看前缀时，两种问题效果差不多。这个排序与裁判分析的结论一致：在 Hindsight 下，Value 问题给一个回合中所有动作几乎相同的分数，因此说明不了哪些动作有帮助。",
 "Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct, mean of three seeds": "Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct，三个种子的平均",
 "Success rate, teacher-trained policy vs GRPO": "成功率：有老师指导的策略对比 GRPO",
 "<span><i style=\"background:var(--base-2)\"></i>GRPO (outcome reward only)</span><span><i id=\"f7-key\" style=\"background:var(--tea)\"></i><span id=\"f7-name\">Hindsight + Progress</span></span><span>whiskers: ± std over seeds</span>": "<span><i style=\"background:var(--base-2)\"></i>GRPO（仅结果奖励）</span><span><i id=\"f7-key\" style=\"background:var(--tea)\"></i><span id=\"f7-name\">Hindsight + Progress</span></span><span>误差线：种子间 ± 标准差</span>",
 "<b>Figure 7.</b> Success rates (%) of the 1.5B policy trained with JEV as the teacher under each question and context, against GRPO. The last two groups are overall ALFWorld success and WebShop success. Switch settings to compare; Hindsight + Progress is the best setting on both environments. The 7B option shows the same recipe on Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct.": "<b>图 7</b> 以 JEV 为老师、在不同问题和上下文设置下训练的 1.5B 策略的成功率（%），与 GRPO 对比。最后两组分别是 ALFWorld 总体成功率和 WebShop 成功率。可以切换设置比较，Hindsight + Progress 在两个环境上都是最佳设置。7B 选项展示的是同一方法在 Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct 上的结果。",
 "The gain holds at 7B, from 77.6% to 83.8% on ALFWorld and from 66.1% to 73.6% on WebShop, and <strong>the 1.5B policy taught this way outperforms the 7B policy trained with outcome rewards alone on both environments.</strong> Hindsight + Progress also finishes sooner: it completes 74.5% of ALFWorld tasks within 20 actions, against 63.6% to 69.5% for the other settings, and 71.1% of WebShop tasks within 10 actions, against 60.9% to 62.2%.": "在 7B 上提升依然存在：ALFWorld 从 77.6% 到 83.8%，WebShop 从 66.1% 到 73.6%。<strong>用这种方式教出的 1.5B 策略，在两个环境上都超过了只用结果奖励训练的 7B 策略。</strong>Hindsight + Progress 完成任务也更快：74.5% 的 ALFWorld 任务在 20 步内完成，其他设置为 63.6% 到 69.5%；71.1% 的 WebShop 任务在 10 步内完成，其他设置为 60.9% 到 62.2%。",
 "Learning beyond the teacher": "学生超过老师",
 "On the same ALFWorld evaluation tasks, JEV completes 42.9% as an actor; the 1.5B policy trained on its scores completes 82.9%. <strong>The largest gains are on the dependent tasks, the ones JEV handles worst as an actor</strong>: there the policy reaches 86.8%, 6.9 to 16.2 points above the other question and context settings, while JEV itself completes only 14.7% of them (<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-8\">Figure 8</a>). The teacher does not need to solve a task to provide a useful signal for it.": "在同一批 ALFWorld 评估任务上，JEV 作为执行者完成 42.9%，用它的打分训练出的 1.5B 策略完成 82.9%。<strong>提升最大的是依赖任务，也就是 JEV 作为执行者最不擅长的那些</strong>：策略在这些任务上达到 86.8%，比其他问题与上下文设置高 6.9 到 16.2 个百分点，而 JEV 自己只能完成其中的 14.7%（<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-8\">图 8</a>）。老师不需要自己会做一个任务，也能为它提供有用的信号。",
 "ALFWorld, same evaluation tasks": "ALFWorld，同一批评估任务",
 "JEV acting vs the 1.5B policy JEV taught": "JEV 自己执行，对比它教出的 1.5B 策略",
 "<span><i style=\"background:var(--act)\"></i>JEV as actor</span><span><i style=\"background:var(--tea)\"></i>1.5B policy trained with JEV (Hindsight + Progress)</span>": "<span><i style=\"background:var(--act)\"></i>JEV 作执行者</span><span><i style=\"background:var(--tea)\"></i>以 JEV 为老师训练的 1.5B 策略（Hindsight + Progress）</span>",
 "<b>Figure 8.</b> Success rates (%) by task type. The arrow runs from JEV acting on its own (Table 2) to the policy it taught (Table 3). The policy surpasses its teacher everywhere except <i>Pick2</i>, and by the widest margins on the three dependent types.": "<b>图 8</b> 各任务类型上的成功率（%）。箭头从 JEV 自己执行的结果（表 2）指向它教出的策略（表 3）。除 <i>Pick2</i> 外，策略在所有类型上都超过了老师，在三类依赖任务上领先最多。",
 "<strong>Cost.</strong> We query JEV through OpenRouter at 0.042 USD per million input tokens to score every executed action during training: 150 steps, 16 tasks per batch, 8 rollouts per task. Scoring an entire training run costs between 22.21 and 30.07 USD.": "<strong>成本。</strong>我们通过 OpenRouter 调用 JEV，价格为每百万输入 token 0.042 美元，训练中给每个执行过的动作打分：共 150 步，每批 16 个任务，每个任务 8 条 rollout。一次完整训练的打分费用在 22.21 到 30.07 美元之间。",
 "Hindsight + Progress run": "Hindsight + Progress 训练",
 "Max actions per rollout": "每条 rollout 的最大动作数",
 "Teacher API cost (USD)": "老师 API 费用（美元）",
 "<span class=\"n\">5</span>Takeaways for using decision models in agents": "<span class=\"n\">5</span>在智能体中使用决策模型的几点结论",
 "<strong>Actors know the required step but are drawn to the easier one.</strong> They choose the right step when it is the only subgoal, and general reminders do not stop the error. When a decision model must act, restructuring the goal into ordered subgoals is more promising than adding instructions.": "<strong>执行者知道该做哪一步，却会被较容易的那一步吸引。</strong>当必须先做的那一步是唯一的子目标时，它们会选对；通用的提醒阻止不了这种错误。如果必须让决策模型来执行，把目标拆成有序的子目标，比添加指令更有希望。",
 "<strong>The question sets the granularity of the signal.</strong> Asking about the eventual outcome gives every action of a trajectory a similar score and largely repeats the outcome reward; asking about each action's contribution separates them.": "<strong>问题决定了信号的粒度。</strong>问最终结果，轨迹中每个动作的得分都差不多，基本是在重复结果奖励；问每个动作的贡献，才能把它们区分开。",
 "<strong>Hindsight targets the actor's own failure.</strong> Seeing the whole trajectory lets a judge credit the steps toward the subgoal that must come first. Decision models are best used to score actions after an episode, as in RL training, and are less suited to filtering actions online, where only the prefix exists.": "<strong>Hindsight 正好针对执行者自身的失败。</strong>看到完整轨迹，裁判就能给推进必须先完成的子目标的那些步骤记功。决策模型最适合在回合结束后给动作打分，比如在 RL 训练中；不太适合在线筛选动作，因为那时只有前缀。",
 "<strong>Screen judges before training.</strong> Judging recorded trajectories identified the question and context that trained the best policy, at a small fraction of the cost of an RL run. Choose a teacher by how well it judges, not by how well it acts.": "<strong>训练前先筛选裁判。</strong>通过评判已记录的轨迹，我们找到了能训练出最佳策略的问题和上下文，成本只是一次 RL 训练的一小部分。选老师要看它评判得好不好，而不是执行得好不好。",
 "<strong>Step-level supervision becomes affordable.</strong> A frozen decision model, queried after each episode and absent at test time, costs tens of dollars per run and lets a small policy outperform a larger one trained on outcomes alone.": "<strong>步级监督变得用得起了。</strong>冻结的决策模型只在每个回合结束后调用，测试时不需要，每次训练只花几十美元，就能让小策略超过只用结果奖励训练的大策略。",
 "The full list of references, the prompts and the appendix experiments are in the <a class=\"tx\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.17167\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">paper</a>.": "完整参考文献、提示词和附录实验见<a class=\"tx\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.17167\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">论文</a>。",
 "Three robots in a watercolour landscape: an amber actor weighing which path to take, a blue judge inspecting footsteps with a magnifying glass, and a green teacher pointing at a board for a smaller student robot": "水彩风景中的三个机器人：琥珀色的执行者在掂量走哪条路，蓝色的裁判拿着放大镜查看脚印，绿色的老师指着黑板给一个小机器人讲课。",
 "Role": "角色",
 "Show": "显示",
 "Goal": "目标",
 "Judge": "裁判",
 "s sub i t equals D of g, tau i, t, between 0 and 1; A sub i t equals A out plus lambda times s sub i t minus s bar": "s 下标 i t 等于 D 作用于 g、tau i、t，取值在 0 到 1 之间；A 下标 i t 等于 A out 加上 lambda 乘以 s 下标 i t 与 s bar 之差",
 "Teacher setting": "老师设置",
